description:
Tracker only; no PR.

1. For each open item in astro-site-21, 22, 33, 34, 35, 36, 40, 50, 51, 52 and 53:
   - read its acceptance;
   - finish it only when live evidence (run ids, receipt digests, PR links) shows the acceptance is met;
   - record that evidence in the item's context.
   Otherwise add a note naming the `site-split-*` item that now covers the remaining work.
2. Fold astro-site-54, dlv2-61 and dlv2-62 into this batch. Add a context line mapping each of their steps to the owning `site-split-*` item. Drop each one, with that reason, only after its mapped scope has merged; the batch's final step does this.
3. Record the owner decisions, verbatim with their dates:
   - D11 on astro-site-54: Sphinx rollback retention waived at cutover, 2026-10-06;
   - D7 on dlv2-60: trunk-only docs supersede release-pinned docs;
   - D12 and D18 on dlv2-62.
   dlv2-60 holds a stale expired claim: take it over with a reason, or release it, before finishing or dropping it.
4. astro-site-60 and 61 stay open, with a note that their paths now live in BenchBox-dev/benchbox-site.
